---
import { catalog } from "../lib/catalog.js";
import { formatVerified } from "../lib/format.js";

const verified = formatVerified(catalog.meta.verifiedAt);
---

<div class="notice">
  <p class="data-note-label">About this data</p>
  <p>
    UTQG grades are assigned by the manufacturer under <a href="https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-49/subtitle-B/chapter-V/part-575/section-575.104">49 CFR 575.104</a>.
    Treadwear is a relative grade from a government test course, not a mileage figure.
    Grades from different brands are only loosely comparable.
    <a href="/guides/utqg-grades/">What treadwear, traction, and temperature mean</a>.
    <a href="/guides/treadwear-numbers/">What treadwear numbers mean</a>.
    A tire that is not in the list is covered in <a href="/guides/no-utqg-rating/">why a tire may have no UTQG rating</a>.
    The ratings file has no category field.
    Data last verified {verified} (UTC).
  </p>
  <p>
    The treadwear median is the middle usable grade when the count is odd, and the mean of the two middle grades when the count is even.
    A usable grade is a positive whole number. Size text is shown as NHTSA published it.
  </p>
</div>
